          "id": 23,
          "type": "text",
          "title": "Reading guide",
          "gridPos": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 56,
            "w": 24,
            "h": 16
          },
          "options": {
            "mode": "markdown",
            "content": "## Start with the two status rows\n**Reachable** means the metrics endpoint answered. **Ready** means the service reports that it can do its work. A service can be reachable and still be **Not ready**.\n\n**Unknown** means a sample is missing or too old. Gaps and \u201cNo data\u201d do not mean zero failures. Rates need at least two samples. Open a panel menu, then **Inspect \u2192 Data**, to read its values as a table. Refresh runs every 15 seconds.\n\nChoose a time range above. Expand Automation for background job and control outcomes. The service logs and /ready response provide the next step when a readiness card says Not ready."
          }
        }
      ]
